# DL-SplatGenerator
#
# Two traps learned the hard way in DL-TerrainMapper, and kept here verbatim in
# spirit because both fail SILENTLY:
#   - NO QUOTES around a path. .gitignore treats quotes as literal characters,
#     so a quoted path with spaces matches nothing and the whole folder ships.
#     Spaces need no escaping; only a TRAILING space would.
#   - NO LEADING SLASH unless you mean the repository root ONLY. `/.claude/`
#     never matched `project/.claude/`, which was committed in TerrainMapper
#     v0.1.0 and published the absolute path of Marc's own disk. Bare patterns
#     match at every level.

# ---- PRIVATE: never public, whatever else changes -------------------------
# The user's original footage and everything made from it. input\ and output\
# contain people -- IMG_1779 has a child in most of the clip and is unreviewed
# -- so they stay out of git entirely, not "for now". A public sample scene is
# added deliberately, by name, when one exists (see the status notes).
input/
output/
# Marc's numbered milestone backups and session records: on disk, never in git
history and back up/
# The development record -- test runs, measurements, renders, scenes made from
# footage (people may be in them): kept on disk for the tool's story, never in git
test outputs/
# local editor/agent config; holds absolute, machine-specific paths
.claude/

# ---- THIRD-PARTY PROGRAMS: fetched, not redistributed ----------------------
# COLMAP, Brush, ffmpeg and the face model -- 1.9 GB. Also a LICENSING line,
# not just a size one: the ffmpeg here is the GPL-3.0 build, which cannot sit
# inside an Apache-2.0 repository as-is.
bin/

# ---- REPRODUCIBLE: rebuilt by the tools themselves -------------------------
.venv/
# pipeline intermediates (frames, COLMAP databases, dense workspaces)
work/
node_modules/
# Rust / Brush autotune caches
target/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- OS noise ---------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
